  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preventing and responding to the cholera outbreak in the Central Region of Cameroon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to contain the spread of cholera in the Central region by providing the support  to the affected communities and health facilities in the response using these three strategies: 1. Prevention and Control of the disease; 2. Case management, and 3. Building community resilience and access to potable drinking water and sanitation. This project targets the Central region which is the most affected region in the country; specifically 3,488 households are targeted to receive distributions over the 10 health districts affected by the cholera crisis. The project will reach 20,928 beneficiaries, with an estimate out of which 60% will be women (12,557) and girls and 40% (8,371) men and boys.</narrative>
  </description>
